<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n549" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăcŏpos</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b> , i, m.,
		or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăcōpon</span></b> ,
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-um</span></b> ,
		i, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκοπος</span> (removing weariness, pain, etc.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A kind of stone</i>, perh. <i>crystalline quartz</i> or <i>spar</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37,
				10, 54, § 143</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			f., <i>a plant useful in childbirth</i>,
			also called <i>anagyros</i>, <i><span class="en">id. 27, 4,
				13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aco-pum</span></b>  (sc. medicamentum or
			unguentum), i, n., <i>a
				soothing salve</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 4, 31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 23,
				8, 80</span></i>; <i><span class="en">29,
				3, 13 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>